tion, Evaluation, and Treatment of High Blood Pressure: the JNC 7 report</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>289</volume><fpage>2560</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12748199</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chrysant</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Melino</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Karki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The Combination of Olmesartan Medoxomil and Amlodipine Besylate in Controlling High Blood Pressure: COACH, a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 8-week factorial efficacy and safety study</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>587</fpage><lpage>604</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18498909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cushman</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cutler</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Success and predictors of blood pressure control in diverse North American settings: the antihypertensive and lipid-lowering treatment to prevent heart attack trial (ALLHAT)</article-title><source>J Clin Hypertens (Greenwich)</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>404</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12461301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Is fixed combination therapy appropriate for initial hypertension treatment?</article-title><source>Curr Hypertens Rep</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>278</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12117454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frampton</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Curran</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Aliskiren: a review of its use in the management of hypertension</article-title><source>Drugs</source><volume>67</volume><fpage>1767</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17683174</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franklin</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Predominance of isolated systolic hypertension among middle-aged and elderly US hypertensives: analysis based on National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES) III</article-title><source>Hypertension</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>869</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11244010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franklin</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Is there a preferred antihypertensive therapy for isolated systolic hypertension and reduced arterial compliance?</article-title><source>Curr Hypertens Rep</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10981158</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-vhrm-4-1315"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fung</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>J</given-na